(Bug #127: the leading-dot precision branch of `read_format_spec` returned
 before #126's catch-all ever saw the clause, so `{n:.z}` rendered as a
 bare `{n}` with no diagnostic - `z` is not a digit, so there is no
 precision here at all, and the table has no other shape a bare `.`
 clause could be.)

a number called n is 255.
Print "{n:.z}".
